(15. A License to Act) Tj
T*
(Source: Jim Nielsen?s Blog | Published: Sun, 09 Aug 2026 19:00:00 GMT) Tj
T*
(Link: https://blog.jim-nielsen.com/2026/license-to-act/) Tj
T*
(In the past, search engines and the open web granted access to other people?s knowledge but the) Tj
T*
(task fell to you to synthesize an understanding from it and build a capability to act. Now with) Tj
T*
(LLMs, it?s possible to build things you don?t fully understand which then require a perpetual) Tj
T*
(license in order to have the capacity to maintain and modify. LLMs don?t just do things for) Tj
T*
(you, they do things instead of you ? and the doing is a huge part of the point. The struggle to) Tj
T*
(understand, to synthesize, to explain, it all has a byproduct: you! Your own capacity to act in) Tj
T*
(the world. But now you can rent that capacity. Every time you reach for the LLM instead of) Tj
T*
(struggling through it yourself, you?re borrowing against someone else?s capacity that you?re) Tj
T*
(not developing in yourself. It?s as if I used to be a car mechanic , fixing my own vehicles or) Tj
T*
(looking to other mechanics for advice or a demonstration on approaching my problems. That) Tj
T*
(process produced a working car ? the output I wanted ? but it also produced a capability within) Tj
T*
(myself to fix the next one that came along. But now, for expedience and speed, I drop all my) Tj
T*
(cars off the LLM dealer for fixes and maintenance. Fast and efficient ?...) Tj
